//- app/views/privacy.pug
extends layout

block content
  .auth-page
    h1 Privacy notice

    p This page explains what GameTips Forum stores about you and what we do with it. The forum is built around the principle of "minimum data for the job".

    h2 Data we collect
    ul
      li Your chosen username and email address (used for login).
      li Your password, stored only as a bcrypt hash — never in plain text.
      li Optional bio text that you provide.
      li Posts, comments, votes, reports, and direct messages that you create.
      li The timestamp on which you created your account and each piece of content.

    h2 What we do not collect
    ul
      li We do not collect your real name, address, phone number, or date of birth.
      li We do not run third-party advertising trackers or analytics.
      li We do not share data with third parties.

    h2 Cookies
    p The forum sets a single cookie used to keep you logged in. It is HTTP-only (so client-side JavaScript cannot read it) and expires after 24 hours.

    h2 Your rights
    ul
      li 
        strong Access — 
        | Your profile page (#[code /users/:id]) shows the public data we hold about you. The 
        a(href="/account") account settings page
        |  shows everything else.
      li 
        strong Erasure — 
        | You can permanently delete your account at any time from the 
        a(href="/account") account settings page
        | . This removes your account and every piece of content you created (cascaded automatically by foreign keys).
      li 
        strong Correction — 
        | You can edit your posts and comments yourself. Bio and email changes are not yet exposed in the UI for this sprint.

    h2 Contact
    p This is a coursework project, not a production service. If you have questions, raise them with the project team via the 
      a(href="https://github.com/ionvicol/software-engineering-project") GitHub repository
      | .
